+
+## Error codes
+
+| Status | `code` | Meaning |
+| ------ | ------ | ------- |
+| 400 | `invalid_code_format` | Pairing code not exactly 6 digits |
+| 401 | `invalid_pairing_code` | Unknown/expired/consumed/inactive pairing code (no oracle) |
+| 401 | `invalid_token` | Missing/invalid/expired JWT, inactive totem or preset, entity mismatch |
+| 403 | `forbidden` | Entity slug ≠ token entity, or queue outside the effective scope |
+| 403 | `entity_suspended` | Reserved; billing does not exist yet, never sent |
+| 404 | `queue_not_found` | Queue slug not found within the entity |
+| 422 | `inactive_queue` | Queue exists in scope but is inactive |
+| 422 | `invalid_priority` | Priority not one of the backend-owned values (nothing created) |
+| 429 | `rate_limited` | Throttle exceeded (pairing 10/min, issuance 30/min) |
 
 ## Open questions
 
-- [ ] JWT TTL/refresh strategy.
-- [ ] Exact `appearance` / `visual` schema per queue/priority (color/icon/order set).
-- [ ] `totems.api_token_hash` vs JWT `jti` — store hash for revocation lookup.
-- [ ] `totem_presets` + `totem_preset_queue` migration (`php artisan make:migration`) + `database-schema.md` follow-up.
+- [ ] JWT refresh strategy (current: fixed TTL, re-pair on expiry).
+- [ ] Exact `appearance` schema per preset (color/icon/order set beyond the queue/priority defaults above).
 - [ ] Is the number of presets per entity limited by plan (`max_queues`-style)?
+- [x] `totems` + `totem_presets` + `totem_preset_queue` migrations — done.
+- [x] Login response carries the entity pair (`slug` for later calls).
